# Explicit, reviewed vulnerability quarantines for the ci-local trivy gate (gate_trivy mounts this
# file from the committed tree it is judging and passes it via --ignorefile). Every entry must
# carry: why it is not fixable today, why the real risk is acceptable, and the BACKLOG done-when
# that retires it. An entry with no justification is a gate bypass — reject it in review.

# No active quarantines. CVE-2026-14257 (brace-expansion DoS) was retired 2026-08-02: upstream
# backported the fix to the 1.x and 2.x lines (1.1.17 / 2.1.3, published 2026-07-28..30), which the
# original entry could not assume because only v5.0.8 existed at the time and v5 changed the export
# shape. `npm update brace-expansion` moved every copy clear (1.1.18 / 2.1.4 / 5.0.9) without a
# major bump, so the minimatch@3/@5 breakage that blocked it never came into play.
